    "body": "Clarify how to install and invoke the Rust Core tools and the separate Node beta package. The documentation uses an explicit Rust executable and an absolute installed Node entrypoint, and preserves the current profile walkthrough.\n\nThis contains only the two documentation changes from PR246. Its older financial-prefix ancestry is excluded; that work remains separate.\n\nValidation on e6832061:24 current source pins,31 relative links,11 bash syntax blocks, patch dry-run and preserved-walkthrough checks passed. Installation, builds and documented product commands were not executed.\n\nFresh whole source/static-result review is pending. This draft follows PR228; merging requires its parent to reach main and the exact checked tree to match.\n\n\n### Current source and result review\n\nFresh review of exact head `e6832061db2dbdf7206e7a99081b5ef00f53fb53` and its current static result is now qualified and adopted. The 3.888-second check passed: 24 context pins, 31 links, 11 shell syntax blocks and patch dry-run. Installation, package build and all documented runtime commands remain UNRUN. The review retains the stated workspace, shell, UTF-8 and session-lifetime limits. Exactly two documentation files change; financial-prefix work is excluded.\n\nThe exact published stack still requires parent delivery and verified main-tree equality before merge. No wider EARS, native or target exit is closed by this PR.\n",
